IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- THE CORE: the shared nouns, and nothing else (DECLARE, and two constants).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from legislation.gov.uk
-- (point in time 2026-07-08). It is not the official text, and nothing here is
-- "verified against the official text". The rendering OMITS the Act's tables
-- (s 9A(3), s 21(2), Schedule 4 and others): see PLAN.md.
--
-- Rules of use (PLAN.md has the whole list):
--   * a part never edits this file; it defines what it lacks under its own
--     section prefix and records it in NEEDS-CORE.md;
--   * money is a NUMBER in pounds sterling, a weekly figure unless its name says
--     otherwise; a date is a DATE, written `Date day month year`;
--   * a field here is a fact a witness of ordinary competence could testify to;
--     whether the fact makes a section apply is a rule and lives with that section;
--   * numbers that regulations, not the Act, supply (the s 5 limits, benefit
--     rates in Schedule 4, "prescribed" figures) are INPUTS, never typed in here.
-- `daydate` already defines Monday .. Sunday, January .. December and May as
-- NUMBER constants, so no constructor below uses those words.

§ `The shared nouns`

§§ `People`

-- The Act speaks of a "woman" and a "man" (ss 37, 48B, 164 ...). s 140A(5) defines "woman" for
-- that section alone, and no section defines "man". The person states which word applies to them.
-- src:2918 | “woman” means a female of any age.
@ref s 140A(5) (src:2918)
DECLARE Sex IS ONE OF
    Woman
    Man

-- Legal status as a witness would state it (ss 36-42 widows and widowers, ss 48-48C Category B).
-- Living together as if married is a fact about a couple, below, not a status.
DECLARE `Marital status` IS ONE OF
    `neither married nor in a civil partnership`
    `married`
    `in a civil partnership`
    `widowed or a surviving civil partner`
    `divorced or a former civil partner`

-- "pensionable age" is borrowed: s 122(1) sends it to paragraph 1 of Schedule 4 to the
-- Pensions Act 1995, which is not among the sources. So the date the person attains it
-- is a FACT about the person that every part takes as given (as the Act's words
-- "over", "under" and "has attained" are s 173, in ssc-definitions.l4).
DECLARE Person HAS
    `date of birth`                    IS A DATE
    `sex`                              IS A Sex
    `marital status`                   IS A `Marital status`
    `date of attaining pensionable age` IS A DATE

-- s 137(1) "couple" is a rule (ssc5); these are the facts it reads.
-- The two members are married to, or civil partners of, each other; or are living
-- together as if they were a married couple or civil partners.
DECLARE Couple HAS
    `one member`                  IS A Person
    `the other member`            IS A Person
    `married to each other`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `civil partners of each other` IS A BOOLEAN
    `members of the same household` IS A BOOLEAN
    `living together as if married or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN

-- A child in respect of whom a person claims. Which age makes a person a "child"
-- differs by Part (16 in ss 137 and 142, 18 in Part 12ZD): the age is not a field here.
DECLARE Child HAS
    `date of birth`                           IS A DATE
    `living with the person claiming for them` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Employment`

-- s 7(1)(b): for an office the secondary contributor is the person prescribed or the "government
-- department, public authority or body of persons" paying the earnings; ss 115, 161, 169 and
-- 171ZH speak of the Crown.
DECLARE `Kind of employer` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a company or other body corporate`
    `a government department, public authority or other body of persons`
    `the Crown`

DECLARE `Category of earner` IS ONE OF
    `employed earner`
    `self-employed earner`

DECLARE Employment HAS
    `the employee`                 IS A Person
    `the kind of employer`         IS A `Kind of employer`
    `the employment began on`      IS A DATE
    `the employment ended on`      IS A MAYBE DATE
    `held under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `held in an office`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `carried on in Great Britain`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- The facts that ss 164, 171ZA, 171ZB, 171ZL and 171ZU-171ZZ ask in the same shape.
-- "the relevant week" is a different week in each section; each section says which.
DECLARE `Service for statutory pay` HAS
    `weeks of continuous employment with the employer ending with the relevant week` IS A NUMBER
    `normal weekly earnings in pounds over the period the section names`            IS A NUMBER
    `the last day of the relevant week`                                             IS A DATE

§§ `Contributions and earnings`

-- s 1(2)
DECLARE `Class of contribution` IS ONE OF
    `Class 1 primary`
    `Class 1 secondary`
    `Class 1A`
    `Class 1B`
    `Class 2`
    `Class 3`
    `Class 3A`
    `Class 4`

DECLARE `Tax year` HAS
    `calendar year in which it begins` IS A NUMBER      -- 6 April of that year; "1978-79" is 1978

DECLARE `Tax week` HAS
    `the tax year`                    IS A `Tax year`
    `number of the week in the year`  IS A NUMBER       -- 1 to 53: the last day (two in a leap year) is a week

-- s 5(1): for every tax year, these are "the amounts specified for that year by regulations",
-- so they are never in this text: an INPUT, per tax year. Pounds per week.
DECLARE `Earnings limits` HAS
    `the tax year`          IS A `Tax year`
    `lower earnings limit`  IS A NUMBER
    `primary threshold`     IS A NUMBER
    `upper earnings limit`  IS A NUMBER
    `secondary threshold`   IS A NUMBER

-- s 6(1): earnings are paid "in any tax week ... in respect of any one employment".
DECLARE `Earnings paid` HAS
    `the amount in pounds`        IS A NUMBER
    `the tax week they were paid in` IS A `Tax week`

-- s 122(1) "the upper accrual point" is £770 (and a number the Act states, not a regulation's).
-- src:2623 | “the upper accrual point” is £770;
@ref s 122(1) (src:2623)
`the upper accrual point` MEANS 770

§§ `Benefits and payments`

-- Every benefit or payment the Act names. ss 20(1), 63, 94(2), 123(1), 138, 141, 148, 140A.
-- Blank in this text and so not named: severe disablement allowance (ss 68-69),
-- bereavement payment and allowance (ss 36, 39B), unemployment, sickness and invalidity benefit.
DECLARE Benefit IS ONE OF
    `short-term incapacity benefit`
    `long-term incapacity benefit`
    `maternity allowance`
    `widowed mother's allowance`
    `widow's pension`
    `widowed parent's allowance`
    `Category A retirement pension`
    `Category B retirement pension`
    `shared additional pension`
    `child's special allowance`
    `attendance allowance`
    `carer's allowance`
    `disability living allowance`
    `guardian's allowance`
    `Category C retirement pension`
    `Category D retirement pension`
    `age addition`
    `disablement benefit`
    `reduced earnings allowance`
    `retirement allowance`
    `industrial death benefit`
    `unemployability supplement`
    `income support`
    `housing benefit`
    `council tax benefit`
    `community care grant`
    `crisis loan`
    `budgeting loan`
    `maternity expenses payment`
    `funeral expenses payment`
    `cold weather payment`
    `health in pregnancy grant`
    `child benefit`
    `Christmas bonus`

-- Paid by the employer (Parts XI to 12ZE), not by the State; ss 151, 164, 171ZA, 171ZL, 171ZU ...
DECLARE `Statutory payment` IS ONE OF
    `statutory sick pay`
    `statutory maternity pay`
    `statutory paternity pay`
    `statutory adoption pay`
    `statutory shared parental pay`
    `statutory parental bereavement pay`
    `statutory neonatal care pay`

DECLARE Claim HAS
    `the claimant`          IS A Person
    `the benefit claimed`   IS A Benefit
    `the date of the claim` IS A DATE

-- Who decides, pays or is told. The individual's seat never speaks for any of them.
DECLARE Authority IS ONE OF
    `the Secretary of State`
    `the Treasury`
    `the Commissioners of Inland Revenue`
    `a local authority`
    `a billing authority`
    `a social fund officer`
    `the Northern Ireland Department`

-- What an encoded rule is answering (the seat's questions group by this).
DECLARE `Kind of decision` IS ONE OF
    `whether a contribution is payable`
    `whether a person is entitled`
    `how much is payable`
    `for how long it is payable`
    `whether it is disqualified, suspended, reduced or ended`
    `how a person is treated, or what a term means`

§§ `Time`

DECLARE Period HAS
    `the first day` IS A DATE
    `the last day`  IS A DATE

-- "week" has six meanings in this Act, and the part that uses one says which.
-- src:2624 | “week” ... means a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday;
-- src:2833 | “week”, in relation to council tax benefit, means a period of 7 days beginning with a Monday.
-- src:3225 | “week” means any period of 7 days.
-- src:3300 | (8) In subsections (1), (4) and (6) “week” means a period of seven days beginning with the day of the week on which the maternity pay period begins.
-- src:3369 | (1A) In this Part, except section 165(1), (4) and (6), section 166(1) and paragraph 3(2) of Schedule 13, “week” means a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday or such other period as may be prescribed in relation to any particular case or class of case.
-- src:5421 | (6) In this paragraph “week” means such period of 7 days as may be prescribed by regulations made for the purposes of this paragraph.
@ref s 122(1), s 137(1), s 163(1), s 165(8), s 171(1A), Sch 7 (src:2624) (src:2833) (src:3225) (src:3300) (src:3369) (src:5421)
DECLARE `Week convention` IS ONE OF
    `a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday`
    `a period of 7 days beginning with Monday`
    `any period of 7 days`
    `a period of 7 days beginning with the day on which a stated period begins`
    `a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday or another prescribed period`
    `such period of 7 days as may be prescribed`

§§ `Birth, adoption and placement`

-- ss 35(6) and 171(1) define "confinement" the same way (and ss 171ZA(5), 171ZZ15 speak of a
-- child stillborn after twenty-four weeks of pregnancy); the facts are these.
-- A woman whose labour begun on one day results in the issue of a child on another is
-- confined on the day of the issue (of the last child, for twins or more).
DECLARE Labour HAS
    `weeks of pregnancy when labour began`     IS A NUMBER
    `labour resulted in the issue of a living child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day of the issue of the child, or of the last of the children` IS A DATE

-- src:1018 | (b) labour after 24 weeks of pregnancy resulting in the issue of a child whether alive or dead,
-- src:3353 | labour after 24 weeks of pregnancy resulting in the issue of a child whether alive or dead,
-- src:3398 | (5) In this section, “newborn child” includes a child stillborn after twenty-four weeks of pregnancy.
-- src:4128 | (a) references to a child include a child stillborn after twenty-four weeks of pregnancy, and
@ref s 35(6)(b), s 171(1), s 171ZA(5), s 171ZZ15 (src:1018) (src:3353) (src:3398) (src:4128)
`the weeks of pregnancy named in the stillbirth rule` MEANS 24

-- ss 171ZB(8) and (10), 171ZL(9), 171ZV and the parts after them.
-- src:3414 | (8) This section has effect in a case involving a child placed under section 22C of the Children Act 1989 by a local authority in England with a local authority foster parent who has been approved as a prospective adopter with the following modifications—
-- src:3420 | (10) This section has effect in a case involving a child placed under section 81 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014 by a local authority in Wales with a local authority foster parent who has been approved as a prospective adopter with the following modifications—
@ref s 171ZB(8), s 171ZB(10) (src:3414) (src:3420)
DECLARE `Kind of placement` IS ONE OF
    `placed for adoption under the law of a part of the United Kingdom`
    `placed under section 22C of the Children Act 1989`
    `placed under section 81 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014`

DECLARE Placement HAS
    `the kind of placement`                     IS A `Kind of placement`
    `the day the person was notified of the match` IS A DATE
    `the day the child was or is expected to be placed` IS A DATE
